From 005d8b2e25d644f639d99f227bd9f78d4eac81a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kamal63442 <kamal63442@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:16:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] rework: the left-edge pin anchors to the first shell thing on
 the left (maintainer spec on #554)

erez-c137's review of PR #554: anchor the widget to the FIRST shell thing on the LEFT of the
taskbar - the Widgets/weather button's right edge when it is there, otherwise the bar's left
edge - not the screen edge - and keep LEFT_ANCHOR_GAP_PX (8, its own constant: same rule as
TRAY_EDGE_MIN_GAP_PX, never abut a shell button, but separate so tuning the tray side does not
move this one) off it. Left-aligned bars and Win10-style bars have Start + apps right at the
left end, so the pin falls back to the normal tray spot there; side bars stay out of scope
(the option greys out). Built in from the start:

- the #24 app-overlap yield on that side: _pinned_overlap_context judges the ANCHORED spot
  (the 'pinned to the left edge' exemption string is gone) - the widget hides when the app
  buttons' rect reaches it and returns when room comes back, through the same gate as the
  tray side;
- following the weather button when its width changes: _refresh_left_anchor_layout keeps the
  bar's Widgets box current (a slot probe with a bounded wait on FIRST sight of a bar -
  startup / a TaskbarCreated's fresh HWND - then the background queue at the tray-less
  refresh cadence) and every placement pass re-derives the anchor from it;
- a drag offset measured FROM the left anchor (not tray_offset_x): 'left_anchor_drag_dx'
  (DEFAULT_CONFIG + schema, clamped >= 0 live in constrain_drag so the widget never lands on
  the shell button), saved by the drop and cleared by Reset position (reset_to_default /
  reset_to_default_position), counted by has_custom_position so Reset is offered;
- topmost without a helper: burial recovery in pin mode does NOT re-seat 'directly above the
  taskbar' - it re-asserts HWND_TOPMOST on the widget's own window and re-places AT the
  anchored spot (the pin block re-derives it), with the same guards (fullscreen app, raised
  band) and the same backoff/fresh bookkeeping; the one-time topmost seat at a (re)dock lands
  at the anchor too. Event-driven only (TaskbarCreated, layout changes, burial detection) -
  NO timers, no periodic re-assertion (#200).

Settings: the toggle moves to the Widget page's Behavior section (2.2.1 IA - positioning
lives there), same Win11Toggle + SettingCard pattern, load/save wired, greyed out on side
bars (re-checked on load and on show); PIN_LEFT_EDGE_LABEL becomes 'Anchor the widget to the
left end of the taskbar', mirrored to all 17 locales. PIN_LEFT_EDGE_OFFSET_PX (15) is
replaced by LEFT_ANCHOR_GAP_PX (8); 'Show on all taskbars' mirrors keep pinning to their own
screen's bar (the screen probe is unchanged). tray_manager.py is untouched.
